1
00:00:03,590 --> 00:00:07,190
Wow, Sheldon, I cannot believe you made up your own game.

2
00:00:07,190 --> 00:00:10,390
Oh, "Research Lab" is more than a game.

3
00:00:11,690 --> 00:00:14,350
It's like the slogan says: "The physics is theoretical,

4
00:00:14,350 --> 00:00:16,250
but the fun is real."

5
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:19,890
We must not be playing it right.

6
00:00:20,890 --> 00:00:22,420
All right, five.

7
00:00:22,490 --> 00:00:25,020
One, two, three, four, five.

8
00:00:25,090 --> 00:00:26,350
Oh, wow, look at that.

9
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:29,090
My Department of Defense research grant is renewed.

10
00:00:29,150 --> 00:00:31,090
Oh! Great roll!

11
00:00:31,150 --> 00:00:34,050
Now you can demolish your Soviet-style cyclotron

12
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:36,920
and build the large Hadron Collider.

13
00:00:36,990 --> 00:00:38,920
Yay.

14
00:00:38,990 --> 00:00:41,690
You're a natural at this, Penny.

15
00:00:41,690 --> 00:00:44,520
And as the first beta testers, you two'll have quite the edge

16
00:00:44,590 --> 00:00:46,890
when we play with Wolowitz and Koothrappali on Sunday.

17
00:00:46,950 --> 00:00:48,850
Oh, gee, Sheldon,

18
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:51,290
I don't think we can play on Sunday.

19
00:00:51,350 --> 00:00:52,150
Why not?

20
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:55,290
Because of the reasons that Penny will now tell you.

21
00:00:55,350 --> 00:00:56,720
Penny?

22
00:00:56,790 --> 00:00:59,150
Actually, I have to pick up my friend Justin from the airport.

23
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:01,620
There you go-- she has to pick up her friend Justin at the airport.

24
00:01:01,690 --> 00:01:03,920
And I can't play 'cause I'm going with her-- right?

25
00:01:03,990 --> 00:01:05,250
Um, yeah, if you want.

26
00:01:05,320 --> 00:01:06,750
I mean, there may not be room.

27
00:01:06,750 --> 00:01:09,450
He's got a lot of stuff--like guitars and amplifiers...

28
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:10,650
Wait.

29
00:01:10,650 --> 00:01:12,350
What are you talking about?

30
00:01:12,420 --> 00:01:13,550
My friend Justin.

31
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:14,690
Pay attention, Leonard.

32
00:01:14,750 --> 00:01:15,950
That's why she can't play on Sunday.

33
00:01:16,020 --> 00:01:17,450
Who is this Justin?

34
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:19,190
- Your turn, Leonard.  - I told you about him.

35
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:20,820
- No, you didn't. - Roll the dice, Leonard.

36
00:01:20,890 --> 00:01:23,220
Yeah-- my friend from Omaha; plays the guitar.

37
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:25,220
Anyway, he's coming to L.A. looking for some session work,

38
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:27,450
so I told him he could just crash on my couch for a few weeks.

39
00:01:27,450 --> 00:01:28,490
Come on, Leonard--if you roll a six,

40
00:01:28,550 --> 00:01:30,690
Penny dies horribly in a nuclear meltdown.

41
00:01:31,890 --> 00:01:34,750
See what I mean when I say the fun is real?

42
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:36,920
Hang on.

43
00:01:36,990 --> 00:01:39,150
Some guy is going to be sleeping on your couch?

44
00:01:39,220 --> 00:01:40,490
He's not "some guy."

45
00:01:40,550 --> 00:01:41,720
He's my friend.

46
00:01:41,790 --> 00:01:44,920
So by "friend," do you mean "friend friend,"

47
00:01:44,990 --> 00:01:46,790
"gay friend," or "ex-boyfriend

48
00:01:46,790 --> 00:01:48,050
"who you're now platonic with

49
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:50,320
but still might have a thing for you friend"?

50
00:01:50,390 --> 00:01:53,050
Well, he's definitely not gay.

51
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:55,150
Oh, ho-ho, a definitely not gay musician

52
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:57,120
sleeping on my girlfriend's couch.

53
00:01:57,190 --> 00:01:59,120
Yippee.

54
00:01:59,190 --> 00:02:02,220
Okay, we went out a little bit, a long time ago.

55
00:02:02,290 --> 00:02:04,290
But we were never like "going out."

56
00:02:04,350 --> 00:02:06,550
Okay, not to be pedantic, but last I checked

57
00:02:06,620 --> 00:02:09,550
"went out" was in fact the past tense of "going out"--

58
00:02:09,550 --> 00:02:12,190
which I think we all know is a popular euphemism

59
00:02:12,250 --> 00:02:14,220
for "saw each other naked."

60
00:02:15,190 --> 00:02:17,890
I'll just roll for you.

61
00:02:17,950 --> 00:02:20,250
Do you have a problem with Justin staying with me?

62
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:21,820
What was your first clue?

63
00:02:21,890 --> 00:02:23,850
Uh-oh! Industrial accident.

64
00:02:25,190 --> 00:02:27,750
You know what? Don't talk to me like I'm an idiot.

65
00:02:27,820 --> 00:02:29,220
I'm not talking to you like you're an idiot!

66
00:02:29,290 --> 00:02:31,650
I'm saying the whole idea is idiotic!

67
00:02:31,650 --> 00:02:33,890
"You accidentally stare at a helium-argon laser.

68
00:02:33,950 --> 00:02:36,590
Lose one turn and a retina."

69
00:02:36,650 --> 00:02:38,720
How is that not talking to me like I'm an idiot?

70
00:02:38,790 --> 00:02:40,520
It's my friend, it's my couch,

71
00:02:40,590 --> 00:02:41,520
and it's my freakin' life!

72
00:02:41,590 --> 00:02:43,420
It's also your roll.

73
00:02:43,490 --> 00:02:45,290
You know what? It is your life.

74
00:02:45,350 --> 00:02:47,720
If you want to have some stupid guitarist stay on your couch, then fine!

75
00:02:48,020 --> 00:02:49,750
Why don't you just rent

76
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:52,320
some bunk beds and invite The Black Eyed Peas?!

77
00:02:52,390 --> 00:02:54,950
Hey, if I want to invite the entire lineup of Lollapalooza

78
00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:56,550
to sleep in my apartment, I will,

79
00:02:56,620 --> 00:02:57,750
and it's none of your business!

80
00:02:57,820 --> 00:02:58,850
Are you listening to yourself?

81
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,290
Do you know how childish you sound right now?

82
00:03:00,350 --> 00:03:01,420
Oh, now I'm a child?

83
00:03:01,490 --> 00:03:02,920
Well, at least I'm not an idiot anymore!

84
00:03:02,990 --> 00:03:04,620
The two aren't mutually exclusive!

85
00:03:04,690 --> 00:03:06,250
Oh, you are such a--

86
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:08,250
What the hell is he doing?!

87
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:09,490
He's drowning us out.

88
00:03:09,550 --> 00:03:10,990
He doesn't like fighting.

89
00:03:11,050 --> 00:03:12,950
Sheldon, just stop! Look, the fight is over!

90
00:03:13,020 --> 00:03:14,690
Oh, and FYI,

91
00:03:14,750 --> 00:03:16,490
you never even heard of The Black Eyed Peas

92
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:17,450
until you met me!

93
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:19,520
I heard of 'em!

94
00:03:20,650 --> 00:03:23,050
Didn't know they were a band.

95
00:03:24,150 --> 00:03:25,220
Sheldon, she's gone.

96
00:03:25,290 --> 00:03:26,590
You can turn off the blender.

97
00:03:32,990 --> 00:03:36,720
Has your relationship reached its inevitable ugly end?

98
00:03:37,750 --> 00:03:40,420
No, we just had a little spat.

99
00:03:40,490 --> 00:03:42,090
Look on the bright side.

100
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:44,050
As a result of Penny's forfeit

101
00:03:44,090 --> 00:03:47,820
you have become the world's first winner of "Research Lab."

102
00:03:47,890 --> 00:03:50,820
Would you like a commemorative snow cone?

103
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:21,800
I don't get how she can just announce

104
00:04:21,870 --> 00:04:24,240
that an old boyfriend is going to be sleeping on her couch.

105
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:26,800
Hey, I thought of a game we can play in the car.

106
00:04:26,870 --> 00:04:28,270
I don't want to play a game, Sheldon.

107
00:04:28,340 --> 00:04:29,500
It's called "Scientists."

108
00:04:29,570 --> 00:04:31,540
Now, I will name three scientists,

109
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:33,100
then you will put them in order

110
00:04:33,170 --> 00:04:35,500
of the size of their contribution to their respective fields.

111
00:04:35,570 --> 00:04:37,470
To make this game even more compelling,

112
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:39,600
you must consider only the contribution

113
00:04:39,670 --> 00:04:40,870
of the man to the field,

114
00:04:40,940 --> 00:04:43,140
not the validity of the field itself.

115
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:45,600
For example: Abu Musa Jabir ibn Hayyan

116
00:04:45,670 --> 00:04:48,740
made a greater contribution to the discredited field of alchemy

117
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:51,000
than Halbert Vanderplatt made to neurobiology.

118
00:04:51,070 --> 00:04:52,640
Okay, ready to have some fun?

119
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:56,640
An old boyfriend who's definitely not gay.

120
00:04:56,700 --> 00:04:59,500
That's what a guy likes to hear-- "definitely."

121
00:04:59,570 --> 00:05:01,300
All right, I'll start with an easy one:

122
00:05:01,370 --> 00:05:05,870
Um, Isaac Newton, Madame Curie and Niels Bohr.

123
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:08,600
And then I say one little thing and I end up being the bad guy!

124
00:05:08,670 --> 00:05:11,870
Hint: Madame Curie had her husband to help her.

125
00:05:11,940 --> 00:05:13,370
What am I supposed to say?

126
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:15,770
"Sure, Penny, I'm cool with your old boyfriend

127
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:17,200
sleeping in your apartment."

128
00:05:17,270 --> 00:05:19,370
"Well, Leonard, it doesn't matter if you're cool or not

129
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:20,940
"because I'm Penny and I'm pretty

130
00:05:20,940 --> 00:05:22,540
and I can do whatever the hell I want!"

131
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:24,300
"Oh, I get it!

132
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:26,040
"You think you're doing me a favor just by

133
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:27,200
being in a relationship with me!"

134
00:05:27,270 --> 00:05:28,740
"No, no, Leonard! I'doing you a favor

135
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:30,200
just by being in the same room as you!"

136
00:05:30,270 --> 00:05:31,570
Leonard! Stop the car!

137
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,500
What?

138
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:36,800
I can't listen to the two of you fight anymore.

139
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:43,600
Come on, come on, we're late.

140
00:05:43,670 --> 00:05:45,100
Calm down. We'll make the movie.

141
00:05:45,140 --> 00:05:47,700
I believe my alarm is appropriate,given the situation.

142
00:05:47,770 --> 00:05:49,540
The movie starts in 17 minutes,

143
00:05:49,540 --> 00:05:51,540
which means we'll need to make all the lights

144
00:05:51,540 --> 00:05:53,940
on Colorado Boulevard, plus skip the concession stand,

145
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,300
and preshow urination.

146
00:05:55,370 --> 00:05:58,240
Oh, dude, I wish you had said something

147
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:00,840
before I pounded that last Red Bull.

148
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:02,940
Go, go, Power Rangers, go!

149
00:06:05,470 --> 00:06:06,500
Hey.

150
00:06:06,570 --> 00:06:08,140
Hey.

151
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:09,770
We're, uh, going to the movies.

152
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:10,970
No, we're not.

153
00:06:12,070 --> 00:06:13,040
We're standing in the hallway,

154
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:15,770
suffering through an awkward encounter.

155
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:17,700
Hang on.

156
00:06:17,770 --> 00:06:20,200
They're showing a new digital print of Time Bandits.

157
00:06:20,270 --> 00:06:21,600
You wouldn't want to come, would you?

158
00:06:21,670 --> 00:06:23,200
Not really, no.

159
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:25,000
All right, invitation pointlessly offered,

160
00:06:25,070 --> 00:06:26,470
invitation declined as expected,

161
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:27,600
everyone's civil, nobody's fighting.

162
00:06:27,670 --> 00:06:28,670
Have a nice evening.

163
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:32,940
Just give us a minute.

164
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,970
Oh, take all the time you need.

165
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:41,870
So, are we going to talk about last night?

166
00:06:41,940 --> 00:06:44,200
Are you ready to apologize?

167
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:45,230
No.

168
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:46,100
Wrong answer.

169
00:06:46,170 --> 00:06:47,100
But thank you for playing.

170
00:06:47,170 --> 00:06:49,070
Oh, come on.

171
00:06:49,140 --> 00:06:50,240
This is stupid.

172
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:51,270
Oh, there it is again!

173
00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:52,340
You think I'm stupid!

174
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:53,470
No, there's a difference

175
00:06:53,540 --> 00:06:55,170
between being stupid and acting stupid.

176
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,370
Oh, yeah? well, there's a difference

177
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:58,240
between being a jerk and being an ass!

178
00:06:58,300 --> 00:07:00,470
No, there isn't!

179
00:07:00,540 --> 00:07:02,700
They're synonyms!

180
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:07,170
Well, that was rather unpleasant.

181
00:07:07,970 --> 00:07:10,170
Yeah, I don't think I need my preshow urination anymore.

182
00:07:12,170 --> 00:07:14,900
Leonard, when that woman moved in three years ago,

183
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:16,700
I told you not to talk to her, and now look,

184
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:17,940
we're going to be late for the movies.

185
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:25,300
Hey! Look! Amazing Spider-Man 183.

186
00:07:25,370 --> 00:07:27,400
Got it.

187
00:07:27,470 --> 00:07:28,470
Remember this one?

188
00:07:28,530 --> 00:07:29,800
Spider-Man loses a big fight

189
00:07:29,870 --> 00:07:32,300
and then his girl friend breaks up with him.

190
00:07:34,770 --> 00:07:36,330
Want me to get it for you?

191
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:39,200
It'll help take your mind off things.

192
00:07:39,270 --> 00:07:40,870
Hey, guys. What's going on?

193
00:07:40,930 --> 00:07:42,530
Oh, we need to kill a couple hours

194
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:44,430
till the next showing of Time Bandits.

195
00:07:44,430 --> 00:07:46,330
Oh, well,no problem.

196
00:07:46,330 --> 00:07:48,100
I was thinking of closing early and going home,

197
00:07:48,170 --> 00:07:49,570
but let's face it,

198
00:07:49,630 --> 00:07:51,370
that's just a slightly smaller lonely room

199
00:07:51,430 --> 00:07:54,300
filled with comic book

200
00:07:54,370 --> 00:07:57,000
Thanks, Stuart.

201
00:07:57,070 --> 00:07:58,300
Let me ask you something.

202
00:07:58,370 --> 00:07:59,770
Do you think it's okay for Penny

203
00:07:59,830 --> 00:08:01,570
to have an ex-boyfrid sleep on her couch?

204
00:08:01,630 --> 00:08:03,270
No, I mean, she's obviousl way out of line.

205
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:04,270
Thank you!

206
00:08:04,330 --> 00:08:05,630
But if she dumps you,

207
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:07,170
she'll have a new boyfrien by tomorrow morning

208
00:08:07,230 --> 00:08:08,330
and you'll have a new girl friend

209
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:10,330
when you figure out how to build one.

210
00:08:12,470 --> 00:08:15,370
So the only question is: how long until you fold?

211
00:08:15,430 --> 00:08:17,170
I am not going to fold.

212
00:08:17,230 --> 00:08:18,530
Well, excuse me, I don't think

213
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:19,830
Penny's out of line at all.

214
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:21,230
You don't own her.

215
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:23,030
It's like my girl Beyonce says:

216
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:26,570
"If you like it, you should put a ring on it."

217
00:08:27,530 --> 00:08:28,800
Come on.

218
00:08:28,870 --> 00:08:30,000
At the very least,

219
00:08:30,070 --> 00:08:31,330
when she found out Leonard was upset about it,

220
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:33,070
she should've backed off.

221
00:08:33,130 --> 00:08:34,330
You mean like when a guy's upset

222
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:36,000
because his friend agreed to take a cooking class with him

223
00:08:36,070 --> 00:08:37,200
and then doesn't show up

224
00:08:37,270 --> 00:08:39,700
because he's doing a juice fast with his mother?

225
00:08:39,770 --> 00:08:41,970
I didn't know you were upset about that.

226
00:08:42,030 --> 00:08:44,300
Really! Did you miss all the subtitle indicators,

227
00:08:44,370 --> 00:08:46,300
like me saying, "Howard, I am upset."

228
00:08:46,370 --> 00:08:47,570
Okay, sorry.

229
00:08:47,630 --> 00:08:48,970
Maybe it means something different in this country.

230
00:08:49,030 --> 00:08:51,930
Back in India, it means you're upset with a guy named Howard!

231
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:54,030
I said I'm sorry.

232
00:08:54,100 --> 00:08:55,300
Sorry doesn't make up for the fact

233
00:08:55,370 --> 00:08:57,330
that I had to make chicken and rice with this vegan guy.

234
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:59,330
Do you know what vegan chicken and rice is?

235
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:01,370
Rice!

236
00:09:01,430 --> 00:09:03,330
Yeah, well, you think I was having fun,

237
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:05,300
sitting around all night listening to my mother say,

238
00:09:05,370 --> 00:09:08,600
"Have you ever peed so much in your life?"

239
00:09:08,670 --> 00:09:11,530
Oh, my God, you are such a mama's boy.

240
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:14,270
Hey, don't bring my mother into this!

241
00:09:14,270 --> 00:09:15,730
You brought your mother into this!

242
00:09:15,730 --> 00:09:17,230
Stop it, both of you.

243
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:18,970
All this fighting, I might as well

244
00:09:19,030 --> 00:09:20,930
be back with my parents! "Damn it, George,

245
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,230
"I told you if you didn't quit drinkin' I'd leave you!"

246
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:25,030
"Well, I guess that makes you a liar.

247
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:26,830
"'Cause I'm drunk as hell and you're still here!"

248
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:28,000
"Stop yelling!"

249
00:09:28,070 --> 00:09:29,630
"You're making Sheldon cry!"

250
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:31,430
"I'll tell you what's making Sheldon cry!

251
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:33,270
That I let you name him Sheldon"

252
00:09:40,030 --> 00:09:43,000
Boy, what got him so upset?

253
00:09:43,070 --> 00:09:46,000
Oh, sure, you can tell when Sheldon's upset.

254
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:55,530
Oh, thank you very much.

255
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:56,970
Come back soon.

256
00:09:57,030 --> 00:09:58,630
With the other half of my tip.

257
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,160
Hey, Sheldon.

258
00:10:03,230 --> 00:10:04,660
What are you doing here?

259
00:10:04,730 --> 00:10:05,830
This is a restaurant.

260
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:06,960
It's lunchtime.

261
00:10:07,030 --> 00:10:07,630
I would think, as a waitress,

262
00:10:07,630 --> 00:10:09,730
you'd be familiar withhe paradigm.

263
00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:10,900
Is Leonard coming?

264
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:12,860
No, I believe Leonard is waiting

265
00:10:12,930 --> 00:10:15,560
for yo to come crawling back to him and apologize.

266
00:10:15,630 --> 00:10:16,800
Well, that's not gonna happen.

267
00:10:16,860 --> 00:10:18,300
I assumed that would be your attitude.

268
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:19,830
Hence, my true purpose coming here.

269
00:10:19,900 --> 00:10:23,230
- Which is? - I want you to crawl back to him and apologize.

270
00:10:23,300 --> 00:10:24,230
I'm busy.

271
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:26,200
Excuse me, Miss.

272
00:10:26,260 --> 00:10:28,630
I'like to order lunch.

273
00:10:31,630 --> 00:10:33,160
Fine. What do you want?

274
00:10:33,230 --> 00:10:34,760
I have a few questions.

275
00:10:34,830 --> 00:10:37,760
First, I notice that you offer soup and a half-sandwich?

276
00:10:37,830 --> 00:10:39,160
Yes.

277
00:10:39,230 --> 00:10:41,560
Where exactly does the half-sandwich come from?

278
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:43,830
Are you giving me half of someone else's sandwich,

279
00:10:43,900 --> 00:10:45,330
or do I have to wait

280
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:46,630
for someone else in the restaurant

281
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:47,860
to order the other half?

282
00:10:47,930 --> 00:10:50,130
No, no, Sheldon, they just make a half-sandwich.

283
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:51,960
You can't make a half-sandwich.

284
00:10:52,030 --> 00:10:53,960
If it's t half of a whole sandwich,

285
00:10:54,030 --> 00:10:55,560
it's just a small sandwich.

286
00:10:55,630 --> 00:10:58,860
Okay, fine, it's soup and a small sandwich.

287
00:10:58,860 --> 00:11:00,230
that what you want?

288
00:11:00,300 --> 00:11:02,360
Of course not. I'll have my usual.

289
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:03,630
Great.

290
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:06,200
Aren't you going to ask me if I want a beverage?

291
00:11:06,260 --> 00:11:07,230
Don't you usually get lemonade?

292
00:11:07,230 --> 00:11:08,600
- Yes. - Do you want lemonade?

293
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:10,000
- Yes. - Anything else?

294
00:11:10,060 --> 00:11:11,800
Yes-- I want you to apologize to Leonard.

295
00:11:12,260 --> 00:11:14,160
I am not going to apologize.

296
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:15,260
I've done nothing wrong.

297
00:11:15,330 --> 00:11:16,460
He is completely overreacting.

298
00:11:16,530 --> 00:11:17,530
Irrelevant.

299
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:18,800
The disruption in your relaonship

300
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:20,260
is making my life intolerable.

301
00:11:20,330 --> 00:11:23,160
Well, I'm sorry, Sheldon, but this really isn't about you.

302
00:11:23,230 --> 00:11:26,030
I don't follow.

303
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:28,800
ah, yeah, I'll be right there.

304
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:29,800
Look, Sheldon, I have to go.

305
00:11:29,860 --> 00:11:32,230
All right, let's assume, ad argumentum,

306
00:11:32,230 --> 00:11:34,000
that in this case, Leonard is wrong.

307
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:35,530
Leonard is wrong.

308
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:36,960
Considering the number of transgressions

309
00:11:37,030 --> 00:11:38,800
you've committed that he's overlooked,

310
00:11:38,860 --> 00:11:40,230
Don't you think that, just this once,

311
00:11:40,300 --> 00:11:41,260
you could return the favor?

312
00:11:41,330 --> 00:11:42,300
I'm coming.

313
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:43,460
Good-bye, Sheldon.

314
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:51,030
What do you mean, transgressions I've committed?

315
00:11:51,100 --> 00:11:52,330
Were you under the impression

316
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:54,330
that Leonard has no complaints about you?

317
00:11:54,400 --> 00:11:55,930
Like what?! Yeah, yeah, I see you.

318
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,860
You're making a little check sign in the air.

319
00:11:57,930 --> 00:11:59,460
I got it. Just hold you horses.

320
00:12:00,530 --> 00:12:01,700
What does Leonard complain about?

321
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:03,160
Your driving.

322
00:12:03,230 --> 00:12:05,230
The plethora of stuffed animals on your bed

323
00:12:05,300 --> 00:12:07,560
that stare at him during your amorous activities.

324
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:11,330
Your constant tardiness, your singing.

325
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:12,300
My singing?

326
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:13,760
That's actually from my list.

327
00:12:13,830 --> 00:12:15,600
But Leonard would be a fool if he didn't agree with it.

328
00:12:15,660 --> 00:12:18,400
Okay, if Leonard has so many problems with me,

329
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:19,630
Why hasn't he just said so?

330
00:12:19,630 --> 00:12:20,600
Because, according to him

331
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:22,230
you're oversensitive and have a temper.

332
00:12:22,230 --> 00:12:23,330
Oh, really?

333
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:24,730
Well, then, do me a favor

334
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:27,130
and tell Leonard that he can drop dead!

335
00:12:30,630 --> 00:12:33,730
And she wonders why she's constantly undertipped.

336
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:40,800
Oh, good, you're home.

337
00:12:40,860 --> 00:12:42,300
I need you to do me a favor.

338
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:42,730
Sure.

339
00:12:42,730 --> 00:12:43,900
Go apologize to Penny.

340
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:47,330
- What?! - Right now would be good.

341
00:12:47,330 --> 00:12:48,900
Leonard!

342
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:51,260
Although, a few minutes ago would have been better.

343
00:12:51,330 --> 00:12:52,700
I hear you don't like

344
00:12:52,760 --> 00:12:56,030
My stuffed animals, my driving or my punctuality.

345
00:12:56,030 --> 00:12:58,260
What? Who would tell you something like that?

346
00:12:58,330 --> 00:13:00,660
Why would you tell her something like that?

347
00:13:00,730 --> 00:13:02,400
It doesn't matter why he told me.

348
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:03,440
It's true, isn't it?

349
00:13:03,500 --> 00:13:04,600
Okay, yeah, it's true,

350
00:13:04,670 --> 00:13:06,140
but I can live with that stuff.

351
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:08,640
What I can't live with is you casually informing me

352
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:10,800
that some guy's going to be staying your apartment

353
00:13:10,870 --> 00:13:11,970
wiout even asking me first!

354
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:13,200
That isn't your problem!

355
00:13:13,270 --> 00:13:15,000
Your problem is you don't trust me!

356
00:13:15,070 --> 00:13:16,170
Oh, come on.

357
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:17,830
Sheldon, have you ever once heard me say

358
00:13:17,830 --> 00:13:19,500
that I don't trust Penny?

359
00:13:19,570 --> 00:13:21,570
Sheldon? Where did he go?

360
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:22,770
Oh, your yelling

361
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:24,140
Must have freaked him out again.

362
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:25,240
Where are you going?!

363
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:26,370
You just walk away

364
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:27,700
- In the middle of aargument?! - No.

365
00:13:27,770 --> 00:13:29,070
I'm going to go find your damn roommate

366
00:13:29,140 --> 00:13:30,200
before he hurts himself

367
00:13:30,270 --> 00:13:31,470
trying to cross the street something!

368
00:13:31,540 --> 00:13:33,470
Why didn't you say so?

369
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:35,800
Oh, now I need your permission for that, too?!

370
00:13:35,870 --> 00:13:37,540
Well, I can't read your mind, Penny!

371
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:38,700
Really? Why not?

372
00:13:38,770 --> 00:13:40,340
You're so smart, and I'm so dumb!

373
00:13:44,170 --> 00:13:45,300
Raj?

374
00:13:45,300 --> 00:13:46,470
Raj?

375
00:13:46,540 --> 00:13:47,800
Raj?

376
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:49,400
Stop knocking! It's open!

377
00:13:49,470 --> 00:13:52,370
Please tell my parents that our Dark Matter research

378
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:54,640
Is at a critical juncture, and I can't come home

379
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:55,840
For my cousin Sanjay's wedding.

380
00:13:55,840 --> 00:13:56,870
Sheldon

381
00:13:56,940 --> 00:13:59,440
Ask our son what we're supposed to say to Mr. and Mrs. Cheldry

382
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:02,270
Whose daughter, Lakshmi is flying in from London,

383
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:03,390
For the sole purpose of meeting him.

384
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:05,140
I didn't ask you to set me up with Lakshmi.

385
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:06,600
You should be thanking us!

386
00:14:06,670 --> 00:14:09,470
Yes.Lakshmi just got her stomach stapled.

387
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:12,970
You have an opportunity to get in good with her

388
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:15,100
Before she loses weight, and her self-esteem goes up.

389
00:14:16,170 --> 00:14:17,540
I don't care!

390
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:20,100
And why don't you think I can find a woman for myself?

391
00:14:20,110 --> 00:14:21,070
Because you're 27

392
00:14:21,080 --> 00:14:22,440
And the closest thing we have to a daughter-in-law

393
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:24,000
Is that Jewish boy Howard.

394
00:14:24,570 --> 00:14:27,670
Oh..that is completely below the belt.

395
00:14:27,670 --> 00:14:30,500
Sheldon,tell my parents that Howard and I are just friends.

396
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:33,500
Sheldon?

397
00:14:33,570 --> 00:14:35,740
Howard and I are just friends!

398
00:14:38,770 --> 00:14:41,940
Fine. I'll come home for Sanjay's wedding.

399
00:14:45,540 --> 00:14:47,140
Sheldon?!

400
00:14:50,470 --> 00:14:51,700
What are you doing?

401
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:52,940
He's not a lost dog.

402
00:14:52,940 --> 00:14:55,200
Hey, why don't you just let me find him

403
00:14:55,270 --> 00:14:57,570
While you sit there hitting your imaginary brake?

404
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:59,340
The brake might be imaginary,

405
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:01,500
But that stop sign you just ran wasn't.

406
00:15:01,570 --> 00:15:02,700
What stop sign?

407
00:15:02,770 --> 00:15:05,600
Eyes on the road. Eyes on the road!

408
00:15:14,740 --> 00:15:18,600
Howard, answer the door! I'm busy!

409
00:15:18,670 --> 00:15:21,270
I'm busy, too! You answer it.

410
00:15:21,340 --> 00:15:23,900
I can't! I'm on the toilet!

411
00:15:23,970 --> 00:15:26,740
For God's sake, I don't need to hear that!

412
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:29,170
Can't you just say, "I'm busy"?

413
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:32,640
I said I'm busy,but that was't good enough for you!

414
00:15:32,700 --> 00:15:35,870
You know what?I hope it's one of those home invasion deals,

415
00:15:35,870 --> 00:15:37,570
And they shoot me in the head!

416
00:15:37,570 --> 00:15:39,240
Well, if it's a home invader,

417
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:41,670
Don't tell them I'm on the toilet!

418
00:15:45,740 --> 00:15:47,770
There's no one there.

419
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:50,270
You're hearing things, you crazy old lady!

420
00:15:52,970 --> 00:15:56,240
Hey, Stuart, have you seen Sheldon?

421
00:15:56,300 --> 00:15:59,100
Yeah, he's, uh, over in the graphic novel section.

422
00:16:00,840 --> 00:16:02,800
Built himself a little nest.

423
00:16:02,870 --> 00:16:04,640
Thank you.

424
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:07,070
- Uh, Penny?  - Yeah?

425
00:16:07,140 --> 00:16:08,470
Is everything okay?

426
00:16:08,540 --> 00:16:09,470
What do you mean?

427
00:16:09,540 --> 00:16:12,070
Sheldon told me you and Leonard were having a fight?

428
00:16:12,140 --> 00:16:14,100
Oh, yeah, kind of.

429
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:15,300
It's-It's no big thing.

430
00:16:15,370 --> 00:16:16,470
Oh, good, good.

431
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:18,500
I love you.

432
00:16:20,270 --> 00:16:22,700
I'm not leaving until you talk to me.

433
00:16:22,770 --> 00:16:23,940
All right, what's going on?

434
00:16:23,970 --> 00:16:26,470
It's a little hard to explain. He does this thing

435
00:16:26,470 --> 00:16:28,340
Where he pretends he's in an alternate dimension

436
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:30,940
That occupies the same physical space we're in,

437
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,970
But he can't perceive us.

438
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:37,470
Don't flatter yourself. I'm just ignoring you.

439
00:16:37,740 --> 00:16:40,470
Come on, Sheldon, let's go home.

440
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:42,240
Look, we're done fighting.

441
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:43,470
I've heard that before.

442
00:16:43,540 --> 00:16:45,270
But then, the next thing you know,

443
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:47,940
I'm hiding in my bedroom,blaring a Richard Feynman lecture

444
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,470
While my mom is shouting that Jesus would forgive her

445
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:52,800
If she put ground glass in my dad's meatloaf.

446
00:16:52,870 --> 00:16:54,640
And my dad's on the roof skeet-shooting

447
00:16:54,660 --> 00:16:58,440
Her Franklin Mint collectible plates.

448
00:16:58,500 --> 00:17:00,600
There's going to no more shouting

449
00:17:00,670 --> 00:17:02,670
And no skeet-shooting.

450
00:17:02,740 --> 00:17:03,840
Really?

451
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:05,770
Where's your friend Justin going to sleep?

452
00:17:06,770 --> 00:17:08,440
Yeah... where's he gonna sleep?

453
00:17:08,450 --> 00:17:11,200
Oh, my God, would you let this go?!

454
00:17:11,270 --> 00:17:12,270
I'd let it go.

455
00:17:13,340 --> 00:17:15,470
Why should I let it go?

456
00:17:15,470 --> 00:17:17,870
Why don't you just tell the guy to find another place to sleep?!

457
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:21,500
Oh, for God's sakes.

458
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:25,240
So, you have childhood issues.

459
00:17:25,300 --> 00:17:27,270
We all have childhood issues.

460
00:17:27,340 --> 00:17:29,940
At some point, you just need to grow up and get past them.

461
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,200
Fire! Fire!

462
00:17:32,540 --> 00:17:34,200
Leonard, will you just let me handle this, please?

463
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:37,240
- Again! Fire! Fire! - Let... just...Look...

464
00:17:42,870 --> 00:17:45,570
Sheldon, please, try and understand.

465
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:47,870
Look, Leonard and I are in a relationship,

466
00:17:47,940 --> 00:17:49,670
And occasionally, we're going to fight.

467
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:52,200
But no matter what happens between us,

468
00:17:52,210 --> 00:17:53,700
We will always love you.

469
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:57,000
Right, Leonard?

470
00:17:57,070 --> 00:17:59,500
Always is a long time.

471
00:18:00,570 --> 00:18:03,400
Sure. Always.

472
00:18:03,470 --> 00:18:05,700
You know, how about we buy you this robot,

473
00:18:05,710 --> 00:18:08,070
And then we all go home?

474
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:10,540
I want that one.

475
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:13,600
Okay, you can have that one.

476
00:18:14,100 --> 00:18:16,170
Oh, come on, he's just going to play with it twice,

477
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:19,440
And then it'll end up in his closet with all the other junk.

478
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:21,640
Buy him the robot, Leonard.

479
00:18:23,640 --> 00:18:25,470
Can I get this comic book, too?

480
00:18:25,540 --> 00:18:26,800
Yes, you can.

481
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:34,800
Meet me again.

482
00:18:42,700 --> 00:18:44,600
So what did Justin say when you told him

483
00:18:44,670 --> 00:18:46,040
He couldn't sleep on your couch?

484
00:18:46,100 --> 00:18:47,270
He'a musician.

485
00:18:47,340 --> 00:18:49,870
He's sleep in his own vomit, if he has to.

486
00:18:59,100 --> 00:19:00,850
I should have asked for much more

487
00:19:00,850 --> 00:19:03,000
Than a comic book and a robot.

